{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"mcp__figma__get_metadata_4_f1d3ab2b","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<canvas id=\"0:1\" name=\"00 · Start Here 设计任务\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"0\" height=\"0\">\n  <frame id=\"3:2\" name=\"Start Here · Brief\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1440\" height=\"2688\">\n    <frame id=\"3:3\" name=\"Header\" x=\"64\" y=\"64\" width=\"1312\" height=\"145\">\n      <text id=\"3:4\" name=\"LEVEL L2 · DESIGN TASK · v2\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"182\" height=\"19\" />\n      <text id=\"3:5\" name=\"Budget — monthly expenses, bills and credit score\" x=\"0\" y=\"31\" width=\"1312\" height=\"52\" />\n      <text id=\"3:6\" name=\"Design a personal budgeting app: see this month’s spending against the budget by category, check the monthly subscriptions, and review the credit score. Canvas 375 × 812, iPhone, light mode. Work in your own new Figma file — this file is read-only reference.\" x=\"0\" y=\"95\" width=\"1312\" height=\"50\" />\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"3:7\" name=\"How to work\" x=\"64\" y=\"257\" width=\"1312\" height=\"227\">\n      <text id=\"3:8\" name=\"How to work\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"147\" height=\"35\" />\n      <text id=\"3:9\" name=\"1. Build exactly the 3 frames below, named exactly as listed (one state per frame), and wire them as a clickable prototype with the listed links. 2. Everything in “Must include” must appear on that frame. The lists are grouped by subject and sorted alphabetically — they are not in screen order and say nothing about layout, grouping, emphasis or styling. Those are your decisions. 3. The brand color and the typeface in 01 · Foundations are fixed. Define every other color yourself, plus type scale, spacing, radii and elevation, and apply them consistently. 4. 02 · Components gives only the platform shell (status bar, home indicator) — this task has no primary button and no text input. Design all other states, the headers, the navigation and every business component as reusable components in your file. 5. Use the service logos and the icons from 04 · Media. 6. Copy and data must match “Fixed data” exactly. This brief wins over anything you may know of the original kit.\" x=\"0\" y=\"51\" width=\"1312\" height=\"176\" />\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"3:10\" name=\"Frames · goals · must include · links\" x=\"64\" y=\"532\" width=\"1312\" height=\"765\">\n      <text id=\"3:11\" name=\"Frames · goals · must include · links\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"413\" height=\"35\" />\n      <text id=\"3:12\" name=\"Frame names are fixed. Must-include lists are grouped by subject and sorted A–Z: they state what is on the screen, never where it goes or how it looks.\" x=\"0\" y=\"51\" width=\"1312\" height=\"22\" />\n      <frame id=\"3:13\" name=\"Frame cards\" x=\"0\" y=\"89\" width=\"1312\" height=\"676\">\n        <frame id=\"3:14\" name=\"01_Expenses\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"644\" height=\"356\">\n          <text id=\"3:15\" name=\"01_Expenses\" x=\"24\" y=\"24\" width=\"116\" height=\"26\" />\n          <text id=\"3:16\" name=\"Goal: See how much of this month’s budget is spent, by category.\" x=\"24\" y=\"60\" width=\"596\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"3:17\" name=\"MUST INCLUDE\" x=\"24\" y=\"90\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />\n          <text id=\"3:18\" name=\"• Budget: “Left to spend” $738 · “Monthly budget” $2,550 · progress of spending against the budget • Categories: Auto &amp; transport · Bill &amp; Utilities, each with icon, total and item rows with amount, amount left and progress (see DATA) • Header: back (Icon_Back) · “Expenses” · add (Icon_Plus) • Main navigation: tab bar Overview / This Month / Offers / Setting · current: This Month • More: more categories (Icon_More) • Period: “September 2020” (Icon_Chevron_Down) · total spent $1,812\" x=\"24\" y=\"116\" width=\"596\" height=\"160\" />\n          <text id=\"3:19\" name=\"LINKS\" x=\"24\" y=\"286\" width=\"33\" height=\"16\" />\n          <tex