egmented control 343×44 with 3 segments, current \"Subscription\".\n\n- `DS/CategoryCard`? Cards differ in item count (2 vs 3). I could make the card a component with 3 rows and hide the 3rd row for Auto. With auto layout, hiding a row collapses it. I'll use auto layout for the card so hiding works. Yes — build with auto layout vertical.\n\nLet me decide to use auto layout extensively for robustness.\n\nDetailed design 01_Expenses (frame 375 wide, auto layout vertical, but screens in benchmarks typically fixed; I'll use fixed positioning for the screen frames but auto layout inside cards):\n\nScreen layout (01_Expenses), bg #F5F6FA:\n- StatusBar instance at (0,0), 375×44.\n- Header at y=44, height 52: back btn at x=16,y=6 (40×40 white circle w/ border); title \"Expenses\" 17px Bold centered; plus btn right at x=319.\n- Period selector at y=112: centered row: \"September 2020\" 15px Medium + chevron down 20px. I'll place centered manually: text width ~120, total ~148, x=(375-148)/2≈113.\n- \"spent $1,812\" — put under period? The must-include: Period: \"September 2020\" (Icon_Chevron_Down) · total spent $1,812. I'll show under the period: \"spent $1,812\" small gray centered. Hmm, or in budget card. I'll do a row: period left, spent right? Classic design: centered period with chevron; below it \"Spent $1,812\" small. Let me do: centered period row y=112; below at y=140 \"Total spent $1,812\" 13px secondary centered? Actually the budget summary card will show progress of spending vs budget which includes spent implicitly. I'll include \"Spent this month $1,812\" inside the budget card too? Avoid duplication confusion. Plan:\n  - Period row centered: \"September 2020 ⌄\"\n  - Below: \"Total spent  $1,812\" centered small (13px, secondary; amount bold ink).\n- Budget summary card y=176, x=16, w=343, h=120, white, radius 20, shadow subtle:\n  - Row: left: \"Left to spend\" label 13px secondary; below \"$738\" 28px Bold ink. Right aligned: \"Monthly budget\" label; \"$2,5