me + detail? Data: name, value, rating, detail. Design: row: left block: name 15 Medium + detail 12 secondary (\"1 missed\", \"-15%\", none for age? Age of credit has no detail — \"Age of credit · 8 years · Good\" no detail). Right block: value 15 Bold + rating pill (Good green / Not bad amber). All text/visibility/fill overrides → single component ×3 instances. \n6. `Comp/ItemRow` — geometry (progress width) differs. Variant approach: property Progress with e.g. 6 variants (47,52,100,93,77)? Ugly but works... Alternatively make ItemRow a component WITHOUT progress bar inside, and add progress bar as separate inline element? But must include \"progress\" in item rows. \n   Option: ItemRow component with auto layout, progress bar = frame track with fill child whose width = variant-specific. Create variants for the 5 needed fills: 47%, 52%, 100%, 93%, 77%. Property \"Fill\" values \"47\",\"52\",\"77\",\"93\",\"100\". Also left-label color override for the $0 case (red) — fills override allowed. This gives genuine reuse (5 instances of one set). Slightly heavy but doable programmatically: create base row, then clone and set fill widths.\n   Hmm, combineAsVariants requires components; create master with children texts/bar, then makeComponent, then clone 4 times, adjust fill width per clone, then combine. Fine.\n   Actually simpler: property values could be semantic: P47 etc. I'll name property \"progress\", values \"47\",\"52\",\"77\",\"93\",\"100\".\n7. `Comp/CategoryCard`? Cards contain ItemRow instances + header; geometry differs (2 vs 3 rows). Two separate components: CategoryCard/2rows, CategoryCard/3rows? Single-use each. I'll skip card-as-component; build cards inline (they compose ItemRow variants + icon instances). Acceptable.\n8. `Comp/Gauge` — single use; build inline as part of score card. Skip component.\n9. `Comp/BudgetSummary`? single use, inline.\n\nI think this is a good balance. Additionally maybe `Comp/PeriodPicker` (month + chevron) single use — inline.\n\nNow screens:\n\n01_Expenses, frame 375×~1130, bg #F5F6FA, clipped.\nOrder with y-cursor:\n- y0: StatusBar instance (375×44).\n- Header instance y=44 (h52).\n- Period row y=108, h=24: centered: text \"September 2020\" 15 Medium ink + gap6 + Icon_Chevron_Down 18 ink. I'll build a row frame width 375 with absolute centered group: measure text width? Use auto layout horizontal frame with layoutAlign center? Create row frame 375 wide, auto layout horizontal, gap 6, align center (counter axis center, primary axis center? primaryAxisAlignItems=\"CENTER\" centers children along primary axis). Yes: row frame w375 h24, AL horizontal, primaryAxisAlignItems CENTER, counterAxis CENTER, children [text, icon]. \n- y+8: \"Total spent\" row centered: text 13 secondary \"Total spent $1,812\" — maybe two-tone: \"Total spent \" gray + \"$1,812\" semibold ink. Two texts in AL row centered. h 18.\n- Budget card y+=16: x16 w343 h124 white r20 shadow. Contents absolute:\n  - \"Left to spend\" 13 secondary at (20,18)\n  - \"$738\" 28 Bold at (20,40)\n  - right: \"Monthly budget\" 12 secondary right-aligned at (right 20, 20) width 120 x=203; \"$2,550\" 15 Bold right at (203,38) w120.\n  - Progress bar: (20, 88) w303 h8 r4 track #EFEFF4; fill 71% → w=215, r4, violet. \n  - \"71% of budget spent\" 11 tertiary at (20, 104)? Let me instead show spent under bar left and \"71%\" right? Keep one line: left \"$1,812 spent\" 11 tertiary? duplication w/ period area... The must-include for Budget: \"progress of spending against the budget\" — bar alone suffices; add small \"71%\" label right side of bar? I'll put tiny \"71%\" above bar right? Simplest: right-aligned \"71%\" 11 tertiary at y=104 x=303-... Let me do row at y104: left \"Spent $1,812\" tertiary 11, right \"71%\" tertiary 11. Duplication acceptable & informative. Hmm period area already says Total spent $1,812. Double duplication. Choose: period area shows \"September 2020 ⌄\" + under it centered \"Total spent $1,812\". Budget card under-bar row: left \"Spent so far\" no... \n    Final: under bar single right-aligned \"71% spent\" 11 tertiary. And no other. Wait \"progress of spending against the budget\" ✓ bar ✓.\n- Credit mini card y+=16: x16 w343 h68 white r16 shadow light: ring: circle 40 at (16,14): outer ring: ellipse 40 with stroke 5 violet bg ring? Mini gauge: ellipse 40×40 stroke #EEEBFD 5; overlay ellipse arc stroke violet arcData 0→0.578*2π rotated -90. Text \"660\" 13 Bold violet centered on it. Texts: \"Credit score\" 15 Medium at (68,16); \"Good · +6 pts\" 12 at (68,38) — green \"Good\"? two texts: \"Good\" green semibold + \" · +6pts\" tertiary. Chevron right at x=311 y=22 20px gray. Prototype link → 03.\n- Section header y+=20 h=20: \"Categories\" 16 Bold at x16; right: nothing.\n- Card Auto y+=12: x16 w343, AL vertical padding 16 gap 14 white r20 shadow:\n  - header row (frame w311 h40): icon chip 40 r12 bg #EEEBFD + Icon_Car violet 24 (resized 22?); name \"Auto & transport\" 15 Bold at x52 y2 (h20); sub \"2 items\"? skip; right \"$600\" 16 Bold right-aligned.\n  - ItemRow instance variant 47 with texts (Auto & transport, $350, Left $186, bar violet).\n  - ItemRow variant 52 (Auto insurance, $250, Left $120).\n  - AL vertical: children rows width fill. ItemRow width 311 fixed = fine.\n- Card Bill y+=16 similar: coral theme; items: Subscriptions $52 Left $0 (100%, left label red), House service $138 Left $10 (93%), Maintenance $130 Left $30 (77%). Card gets reaction → 02_Bill. Also add chevron right on card header to hint navigation? Add Icon_Chevron_Right 18 gray at right next to total. Good affordance.\n- More categories y+=16: dashed bordered frame w343 h48 r14: AL horizontal centered gap8: Icon_More 20 secondary + \"More categories\" 14 Medium secondary. Dash: strokes with dashPattern [4,4], strokeWeight 1, color #C9CCDA.\n- bottom spacer 24; TabBar instance; HomeIndicator instance y=tabbar+64.\n\nCompute total height later in code dynamically: build sections with cursor; at