π). Progress ellipse same, stroke gradient violet→green? Use conic? Use linear gradient horizontal from #6347EB (left) to #2EC4A0 (right)? Actually classic credit gauge: red→yellow→green. Score 660 \"Good\". I'll do progress stroke = gradient [ #6347EB → #8E7BFF ]? Hmm rating colors: good=green. Let me make gauge progress use gradient from #FFB020 (amber) at left through to #27A468 (green) at right — communicates range. Or full-range background ring with gradient (red→amber→green) full half, plus a marker/dot at 57.8% position + gray overlay covering beyond? That's the classic: full gradient semicircle, needle at position.\n    Simpler robust: bg ring light gray (full half), progress ring 57.8% with solid violet, plus end dot. And \"Good\" pill green. I'll go: progress stroke = linear gradient violet #6347EB → #9F8CFF. Looks branded. Needle: small white circle w/ violet border at arc end point. Angle for 57.8%: θ = 180° + 0.578*180° = 284°? In standard math coords with arcData startingAngle measured from positive x-axis. Figma arcData: startingAngle in radians, 0 = 3 o'clock, positive clockwise? Figma's arc angles go clockwise (since y is down). Half ring top: start π (9 o'clock) end 2π (3 o'clock) going clockwise through top (3π/2 = 12 o'clock). Progress end = π + 0.578*π = 2.397? π*1.578=4.957 rad. Dot position: cx=171.5(card-center), cy=center y; point = center + r*(cos θ, sin θ) with θ=4.957: cos=-0.?? cos(4.957)=cos(284°)=0.242? cos(284°)=cos(-76°)=0.2419, sin(284°)=-0.9703. r=110 → offset (26.6, -106.7). Dot at (171.5+26.6, cy-106.7).\n  - Center texts: \"660\" 44 Bold ink centered at gauge center y-10; below: pill \"Good\" green bg #E4F5EC text #1F8A56 12 Semibold r8 padding 4/8; below \"+6pts\" 12 tertiary? Layout: score at center of ring slightly up; pill under score; \"+6 pts since last month\"? data: \"+6pts\". Show \"+6pts\" small under pill? I'll do: \"660\" big, under it pill \"Good +6pts\"? Keep separate: pill \"Good\"; small \"+6pts\" green? Must include both. Row under gauge: \"400\" left, \"850\" right at ring ends; center bottom \"Last update on 20 Jul 2020\" 12 tertiary.\n  - Also labels \"400\" and \"850\" 11 tertiary positioned at ring endpoints (left end at x≈61.5, right end x≈281.5, y=cy+8).\n- Card content plan (absolute):\n  - gauge bg ellipse (220) at x61.5 y28 (cy=138)\n  - gauge progress ellipse same pos\n  - needle dot 14×14 white border violet 4 at computed pos\n  - \"660\" 40 Bold centered (w100 x121.5) y≈100\n  - pill \"Good\" at centered y≈148: frame AL padding(8,4) r8 bg #E4F5EC text 12 Bold #1F8A56; center x.\n  - \"+6pts\" 12 #1F8A56? make tertiary. Under pill y≈180 centered.\n  - \"400\" at (61.5-? ) left aligned x=61.5 y=cy+14; \"850\" right x=281.5-20 y same.\n  - \"Last update on 20 Jul 2020\" 12 tertiary centered y=cy+38.\n  Card height ≈ 28+220+? Let me set card h=320 and tune.\n- \"What affects your score\" section label 16 Bold y after card +24 x16.\n- Factors card: x16 w343 AL vertical white r20 padding 16 gap 16: 3 FactorRow instances + dividers.\n  FactorRow layout (311 wide): left: name 15 Medium; under: detail 12 tertiary (or hidden). right: value 16 Bold at right; rating pill right under value? Row h ~ 48: \n   - name at (0,2) 15 Medium\n   - detail at (0,26) 12 tertiary\n   - value right-aligned at (311-60,2) 15 Bold w60\n   - pill right at y26: AL frame pill with text 11 Bold, padding(6,2) r6; position right: width dynamic... place via measuring? Pill widths vary (\"Good\" vs \"Not bad\"). To right-align, create pill then set x = 311 - pill.width. OK.\n   Row height 48 fixed.\n- TabBar + HomeIndicator at 714/778.\n- Reaction: back → 01.\n\nPrototype reactions:\n- 01: Bill card → 02 (on card frame), credit mini card → 03.\n- 02: back btn → 01.\n- 03: back btn → 01.\nReaction object: {action:{type:\"NODE\", destinationId, navigation:\"NAVIGATE\", transition:{type:\"SMART_ANIMATE\"? or DISSOLVE}, }, trigger:{type:\"ON_CLICK\"}}. For back, use \"DISSOLVE\" or smart animate; simple: transition {type:\"DISSOLVE\", duration:0.2, easing:{type:\"EASE_OUT\"}}? Or null transition = instant. I'll use SMART_ANIMATE for card push, DISSOLVE for back? Keep simple: SMART_ANIMATE everywhere with easeOut 300ms? The API: transition: {type:\"SMART_ANIMATE\", easing:{type:\"EASE_OUT\"}, duration:0.3}. Must have matching layers for smart animate; whatever, it's fine.\n\nAlso flow starting point: Figma auto-creates flow starting points when reactions added? Not automatically via API — need to set? Flow starting points are created in the prototype settings UI; via API there's `flowStartingPoints` on page? Page has `flowStartingPoints` read-only? Actually PageNode.flowStartingPoints is readonly in API. Hmm, can we create? There's no API to add flow starting points historically. Adding a reaction may auto-create a flow start? I don't think so. It's fine — interactions work in prototype when you navigate to a frame; presentation view starts from... without flow starting point, prototype can still be launched? In Figma, if no flow starting point exists, Present picks... you can still play from selected frame. Evaluators typically add/choose starting frame. I'll try to set page.flowStartingPoints? It's read-only (array). Skip; note as limitation if needed. Actually check: plugin API `page.flowStartingPoints` — readonly. Right.\n\nScript size management: I'll do ~4 scripts:\nA) setup page + load fonts + create TabBar, Header, Segments components + helper-created components storage frame.\nB) create ItemRow variants + SubRow variants + FactorRow component.\nC) build 01_Expenses screen.\nD) build 02_Bill.\nE) build 03_Credit_Score.\nF) reactions + final adjustments.\nThen screenshots of each screen, fix issues.\n\nFont loading must happen in each script that creates text (fonts don't stay loaded across plugin runs? Each use_figma call is a new plugin run → must load fonts each time before text ops). Yes, load in every script.\n\nComponent IDs storage: I need IDs across scripts. I'll return JSON of created IDs from each script and pass into next.\n\nLet me also decide shadow style: effects DROP_SHADOW: color rgba(22,22,60,0.06), offset y4, blur 16.\n\nCategory colors: Auto violet #6347EB bg #EEEBFD; Bill coral #FF7A59 bg #FFE9E0. Left $0 red text #E4574C.\n\nRating colors: Good → green (#1F9D63 text, #E3F6EC bg); Not bad → amber (#C77800? use #D97E22 text, #FCF0E0 bg).\n\nText colors: ink #17171C, secondary #6B6F7B, tertiary #9BA0AE. Track #EFEFF4, border #ECECF2, bg #F5F6FA, surface white.\n\nTab bar: white bg, top border 1px #ECECF2 (rect). Icons 24, labels 10 Medium. Current violet, others #A0A4B0.\n\nIcons in tab bar are inside component — recolor at build time in master; instances identical so no per-instance recolor needed. \n\nHeader title override: find text child in instance, set characters. Back/plus identical.\n\nSegments: 343×44 track #EFEFF4 r12 padding 4 AL horizontal; segments fill container h36 r9; current: white fill, shadow, text 13 Semibold ink; others text 13 Medium secondary.\n\nNow — one subtlety: combining variants requires components on the same parent. combineAsVariants(components, parent, index). Then set property names via componentSet. The variant property default name \"Property 1\" → rename: `set.componentPropertyDefinitions`? For variant sets: `set.variantGroupProperties` is readonly; rename via editComponentProperty? Simpler: after combine, `set.componentPropertyDefinitions[\"Property 1\"]` rename via `set.editComponentProperty(\"Property 1\", {name:\"logo\"})`. OK.\n\nCreating instances of a specific variant: get variant component node and createInstance().\n\nText override helper for instances:\n```js\nfunction setText(inst, name, chars){ const t = inst.findOne(n=>n.type===\"TEXT\" && n.name===name); t.characters = chars; }\n```\nName text nodes meaningfully (\"name\",\"amount\",\"left\",\"title\" etc.).\n\nAlso for ItemRow variant: the bar fill widths set per variant at creation. Left label color: default tertiary; for $0 case override fills on \"left\" text (allowed). Bar fill color: default violet; for coral category override fills of fill rect (allowed).\n\nCategoryCard icon chip: build inline per card (icon instance recolored) — fine.\n\nAlright — also the workspace page currently empty (children 0). I'll setCurrentPage to it and create everything there.\n\nOne more: brief says preserve reference pages; I'm only adding to workspace page. Good.\n\nScreens should probably be placed at x spacing: Components area at x=0..375, screens at x=500, 975, 1350, all at y=0. Components area: a big frame \"Budget · UI Kit\" containing components? Components inside a frame: createComponent() adds at page level; then frame.appendChild(comp) works. I'll make container frame \"UI Kit\" w420 AL vertical gap 24 padding 24 bg #FAFAFC? — with variants sets inside too. Frame hug contents.\n\nPosition screens: 01 at x=520, 02 at x=975, 03 at x=1430. All y=0.\n\nLet me now write Script A.\n\nCareful with DM Sans availability — if loadFontAsync throws, fall back to Inter. I'll try/catch and remember family in a variable... but across scripts the family must be consistent. DM Sans is a Google font, available in Figma by default. I'll just load; if it fails I'll see error and adapt.\n\nAlso: text nodes need font loaded before setting characters. Also for instances text override, font must be loaded too.\n\nEdge: createText then setting fontName requires font loaded. Load first.\n\nLet me write Script A now. Also store a JSON \"registry\" — I'll keep IDs in tool results.\n\nRegarding tool-call rate limiting: I've hit the limit message a few times but retries succeed immediately. Continue; if hard-blocked, report.\n\nLet me write the code.\n\n```js\n// Script A\nconst page = (await figma.root.children).find(p=>p.id===\"4:2\") — root.children is sync; figma.root.children.find(...)\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page);\nfor (const s of [\"Regular\",\"Medium\",\"Bold\"]) await figma.loadFontAsync({family:\"DM Sans\",style:s});\n```\nNote: loadFontAsync → figma.loadFontAsync(fontName). Yes.\n\nColors:\n```js\nconst C = { brand:{r:0.388,g:0.278,b:0.922}, ink:{r:0.09,g:0.09,b:0.11}, sec:{r:0.42,g:0.435,b:0.482}, ter:{r:0.608,g:0.627,b:0.682}, track:{r:0.937,g:0.937,b:0.957}, border:{r:0.925,g:0.925,b:0.949}, bg:{r:0.961,g:0.965,b:0.98}, white:{r:1,g:1,b:1}, brandSoft:{r:0.933,g:0.922,b:0.992}, coral:{r:1,g:0.478,b:0.349}, coralSoft:{r:1,g:0.914,b:0.878}, red:{r:0.894,g:0.341,b:0.298}, green:{r:0.122,g:0.616,b:0.388}, greenSoft:{r:0.89,g:0.965,b:0.925}, amber:{r:0.851,g:0.494,b:0.133}, amberSoft:{r:0.988,g:0.941,b:0.878} };\n```\n\nHelpers (define in each script): mkText, solid, shadow, iconInst(compId,color,size), recolor.\n\nTabBar component:\n```js\nconst tabbar = figma.createFrame(); // fixed 375x64, name \"Comp / Tab Bar\"\ntabbar.resize(375,64); tabbar.fills=[solid(C.white)];\n// top border\nconst line = figma.createRectangle(); line.resize(375,1); line.fills=[solid(C.border)]; tabbar.appendChild(line); line.y=0;\n// tabs row: AL frame\nconst row = figma.createFrame(); row.resize(375,64); row.layoutMode=\"HORIZONTAL\"; row.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\"? \n```\nSimpler: 4 tab frames each w=93.75? fractional — use AL with layoutAlign stretch: create row AL horizontal w375 h64, padding 0, primaryAxisSizingMode FIXED, counter FIXED? For children to fill: each tab layoutAlign=\"STRETCH\"? In horizontal AL, child stretch works on counter axis. For primary-axis equal distribution: set each tab's layoutGrow=1 with primaryAxisSizingMode=\"FILL\"? On children: child.layoutGrow=1 makes them share space when parent's primaryAxisSizingMode is FIXED. Yes: parent FIXED w375, children layoutGrow=1 → equal widths.\n\nEach tab: frame AL vertical, counterAxisAlignItems=\"CENTER\", primaryAxisAlignItems=\"CENTER\", gap 3, fills transparent. Children: icon inst 24, label text 10 Medium. Icon recolored per state.\n\nThen tabbar.appendChild(row) — tabbar is plain frame; row at (0,0).\nThen convert tabbar to component: figma.createComponentFromNode(tabbar)? createComponentFromNode exists (converts frame to component). Yes: `figma.createComponentFromNode(node)` returns ComponentNode.\n\nHeader component: frame 375×52 transparent; back chip: ellipse 40 white + stroke border 1 at (16,6); icon back 20 at (26,16); title text width 240 x=(375-240)/2=67.5, align CENTER, y=15, 17 Bold ink, name \"title\"; plus chip at (319,6) ellipse; icon plus at (329,16). Chips as ellipses with shadows? subtle: white fill + border stroke. Name back chip \"back\", plus chip \"plus\".\nConvert to component.\n\nSegments component: frame 343×44 fill #EFEFF4? Use C.track. cornerRadius 12, padding 4, AL horizontal, gap 0. children: 3 seg frames layoutGrow=1, AL centered (primary+counter CENTER), radius 8. current \"Subscription\": white fill + shadow + text 13 Bold? Medium ink; others text 13 Medium sec, transparent. Names \"Bills\",\"Payments\",\"Subscription\". Convert to component.\n\nAlso create container \"UI · Components\" frame? Let me put components into a frame after creation: create frame kit (AL vertical, gap 24, padding 32, fill #FAFAFC? slightly off-white #FCFCFE, radius 24? page bg default is gray; fine), position (0,0), append components. Frame hug.\n\nReturn ids: {tabbarId, headerId, segmentsId, kitId}.\n\nScript B: ItemRow variants & SubRow variants & FactorRow.\n\nItemRow builder (returns frame):\n```js\nfunction itemRow(pct, barColor){\n  const f = figma.createFrame(); f.name=\"ItemRow\"; f.resize(311,64); f.fills=[];\n  // row1\n  const name = mkText(\"Item name\",14,\"Medium\",C.ink); name.name=\"name\"; f.appendChild(name); name.x=0; name.y=0;\n  const amt = mkText(\"$0\",14,\"Bold\",C.ink); amt.name=\"amount\"; amt.textAlignRight=\"RIGHT\"; amt.resize(100, amt.height); f.appendChild(amt); amt.x=211; amt.y=0;\n  // bar\n  const bar = figma.createFrame(); bar.name=\"bar\"; bar.resize(311,6); bar.cornerRadius=3; bar.fills=[solid(C.track)]; f.appendChild(bar); bar.y=28;\n  const fill = figma.createRectangle(); fill.name=\"fill\"; fill.resize(Math.max(6,Math.round(311*pct)),6); fill.cornerRadius=3; fill.fills=[solid(barColor)]; bar.appendChild(fill);\n  // left label\n  const left = mkText(\"Left $0\",12,\"Medium\",C.sec); left.name=\"left\"; f.appendChild(left); left.x=0; left.y=44;\n  return f;\n}\n```\nHeights: text 14px line ~ 18-20 default (lineHeight auto ~ 1.3). Text node height after setting: DM Sans 14 → ~18. y positions: name y0 h~18; bar y26 h6; left y40 h16 → total 56. Set frame h 56. Wait also row name \"Left $186\" at y40 h16 → 56. OK h=56.\n\nMake 5 components: create frame → createComponentFromNode → name \"progress=47\" etc. Then combine: figma.combineAsVariants([c47,c52,c77,c93,c100], kitFrame). Rename property to \"progress\". Set colors: all violet default; for coral items override fill color on instance later (fills override on nested rect allowed).\n\nHmm wait: combineAsVariants parent must be a frame/page; kit frame OK. After combining, instances: get variant node by name \"progress=47\". createInstance() → place in card with x,y. Override texts via findOne.\n\nSubRow builder with logo:\n```js\nasync function subRow(logoId){\n  const f = figma.createFrame(); f.name=\"SubRow\"; f.resize(311,56); f.fills=[];\n  const logoC = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(logoId); const li = logoC.createInstance(); li.resize(40,40); f.appendChild(li); li.x=0; li.y=8; li.name=\"logo\";\n  const nm = mkText(\"Name\",15,\"Medium\",C.ink); nm.name=\"name\"; f.appendChild(nm); nm.x=52; nm.y=8;\n  const pr = mkText(\"$0.00/mo\",12,\"Regular\",C.sec); pr.name=\"price\"; f.appendChild(pr); pr.x=52; pr.y=30;\n  const ch = await iconInst(ICON.chevR, C.ter, 20); f.appendChild(ch); ch.x=311-20; ch.y=18;\n  return f;\n}\n```\nThen components per logo → combineAsVariants → property \"logo\". Instances: override name/price texts.\n\nFactorRow builder:\n```js\nfunction factorRow(){\n  const f = figma.createFrame(); f.name=\"FactorRow\"; f.resize(311,48); f.fills=[];\n  const nm = mkText(\"Factor\",15,\"Medium\",C.ink); nm.name=\"name\"; f.appendChild(nm); nm.x=0; nm.y=0;\n  const det = mkText(\"detail\",12,\"Regular\",C.ter); det.name=\"detail\"; f.appendChild(det); det.x=0; det.y=26;\n  const val = mkText(\"95%\",15,\"Bold\",C.ink); val.name=\"value\"; val.textAlignRight=\"RIGHT\"; val.resize(70,val.height); f.appendChild(val); val.x=241; val.y=0;\n  const pill = figma.createFrame(); pill.name=\"pill\"; pill.layoutMode=\"HORIZONTAL\"; pill.paddingLeft=8; pill.paddingRight=8; pill.paddingTop=3; pill.paddingBottom=3; pill.cornerRadius=6; pill.fills=[solid(C.greenSoft)]; pill.counterAxisAlignItems=\"CENTER\";\n  const pt = mkText(\"Good\",11,\"Bold\",C.green); pt.name=\"rating\"; pill.appendChild(pt);\n  pill.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\"; pill.counterAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\";\n  f.appendChild(pill); // position after measure: pill.x = 311 - pill.width; pill.y=23;\n  return f;\n}\n```\nConvert to single component \"Comp / Factor Row\". Instances override name/value/rating text, detail text or visibility, pill fill (greenSoft→amberSoft) & rating color.\n\nPosition pill after appendChild: pill.x = 311 - pill.width; pill.y = 24.\n\nThen scripts C/D/E build screens, F reactions.\n\nTime to be careful about one thing: setting characters on text inside an instance requires the font loaded in that run — yes we load.\n\nAlso overriding `visible` on instance child allowed. Overriding `fills` allowed.\n\nIcon recolor inside instance: allowed (fills/strokes on nested vectors).\n\nEdge: `li.resize(40,40)` on logo instance — allowed (instance resize at top level of itself, it's a direct child we just created... resizing an instance node itself is allowed).\n\nNow: screens as frames with clipsContent=true, cornerRadius 0? Give them name exactly \"01_Expenses\", \"02_Bill\", \"03_Credit_Score\". Device frame look: maybe cornerRadius 40 to look like device? Reference images probably plain frames. I'll use cornerRadius 0 with bg fill. Actually a phone mock often has rounded corners + stroke. Keep simple: no rounding, just bg.\n\nStatus bar & home indicator: instance of StatusBar (375×44) at (0,0); HomeIndicator at bottom (0, H-34). These are \"not evaluated\" but required on every frame.\n\nLet me now also double check text in brief for header of 02: \"Header: back (Icon_Back) · “Bill” · add (Icon_Plus)\". Yes plus on Bill too.\n\nEntry point for 03: from 01 via credit mini card. ✓.\n\n\"More: more categories (Icon_More)\" ✓ dashed row.\n\nAlso must include on 01: \"Period: “September 2020” (Icon_Chevron_Down) · total spent $1,812\" ✓.\n\nNow write Script A. Keep code compact to stay under 50k chars — fine.\n\nOne more helper: shadow effect:\n```js\nfunction sh(op=0.06, y=4, blur=16){ return [{type:\"DROP_SHADOW\", color:{r:0.09,g:0.09,b:0.24,a:op}, offset:{x:0,y}, radius:blur, spread:0, visible:true, blendMode:\"NORMAL\"}]; }\n```\n\nLet me go. Script A:\n\nAlso I should create text styles? skip.\n\nAfter building everything, screenshots per screen; verify visually; fix issues (likely spacing/text width).\n\nPotential issue: `figma.createComponentFromNode` — exists? The Plugin API has `figma.createComponent()` and `figma.createComponentFromNode(node)` — yes, added in newer API. And `figma.combineAsVariants(nodes, parent)`. OK.\n\nInstance creation from variant: `node.createInstance()` where node is variant component inside a set — allowed, creates instance with that variant selected.\n\nFor Header instance title override & plus hide:\n```js\nconst h = headerComp.createInstance();\nconst title = h.findOne(n=>n.type===\"TEXT\" && n.name===\"title\"); title.characters=\"Bill\";\nconst plus = h.findOne(n=>n.name===\"plus\"); plus.visible=false; // for 03\n```\n\nReactions on nested back chip inside header instance:\n```js\nconst back = h.findOne(n=>n.name===\"back\");\nback.reactions = [{trigger:{type:\"ON_CLICK\"}, action:{type:\"NODE\", destinationId