{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":47656,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"041d6ae8970e0a7a3eacd210e22b0d54","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The icons still render as black squares?! Setting icon still square, back button still black square, chevron down still square. But I just set vector fills and cleared comp fills. The screenshot may have been taken before propagation... but instances are live. Hmm wait — the screenshot render might be cached. Or: my edit set the vector fills on the COMPONENTS — but the instances had OVERRIDDEN fills already (instance.fills = solid ink from recolor). The instance-level fill override still covers the whole instance bounds! Clearing component fills doesn't clear instance overrides.\n\nSo the fix: on all instances, clear the instance's own fills AND set vector fill to the intended color. In Figma, when you change fills on an instance, it becomes an override. To restore the glyph-only look, I must set the vector fills explicitly to the target color and remove the instance-level override (set inst.fills = [] on the instance root).\n\nLet me write a fixer that for each icon instance: \n1. targetColor = current instance fills[0].color (or default ink).\n2. inst.fills = [].\n3. inst.children[0].fills = [solid targetColor].\n\nApply to screens 01, kit, and everywhere. Then colors: tab bar \"This Month\" should be brand — the instance fill was brand (0.388...) so target color preserved. \n\nNote: this month icon shows violet square currently with brand color — good.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"55f02ba1-1af6-4956-ab29-2f9700c86fb2","uuid":"3b84bd9e-74a0-412a-91e8-c45a6d6ffb65","timestamp":"2026-11-02T13:59:02.660Z","thinking_duration_ms":9470}
