instance fills, set vector fill to coral/violet.\n\nAlso check period picker chevron — it renders correctly (small chevron visible). Tab bar icons render. Back button chevron visible. Plus visible.\n\nEverything else on 01 looks great. The credit entry card is below the fold (scrollable) — fine per brief (\"01_Expenses may scroll vertically\").\n\nAlso there's an entry-point consideration: brief says 03 has no entry in the source; I added \"Credit Score entry\" card linking to 03 — good, but it's below the fold. Maybe move it above the categories (right after budget summary) so it's visible without scrolling? That improves discoverability. Actually layout order choice: put credit entry right after budget summary, then Categories label, cards, more row. That keeps visible 812px showing: header, period, budget, credit entry, categories label, first card start. Hmm, that pushes categories down. Either is fine, but visible entry is better for the prototype flow check. Let me reorder: content children order: header, period row, budget, credit entry, \"Categories\" label, cat1, cat2, more.\n\nAlso fix the chip icons. Then final screenshot of 01, and verify 02 & 03 top segments again (02 fine, 03 fine except gauge now ok? — need re-screenshot of 03 to confirm the dial fix propagated to instance).\n\nAlso I should double check that the \"Segments\" instance on 02 now renders text (it did in last 02 screenshot — good).\n\nLet me apply fixes.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"55f02ba1-1af6-4956-ab29-2f9700c86fb2","uuid":"279a7959-103b-4a66-82d8-1621fa821175","timestamp":"2026-11-02T14:25:23.670Z","thinking_duration_ms":46709}
